<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
      Both checks below compare the pinned versions against whatever is newest
      *today*, so their result changes without the source changing — one of them
      (NewerVersionAvailable) even reaches out to the network to do it. That
      makes a lint run non-reproducible, which is the one property a gate needs.

      Dependency freshness is handled deliberately instead: the versions live in
      gradle/libs.versions.toml with the constraints that bind them, and bumping
      them is a change you make and re-verify with `./gradlew assembleDebug`.
    -->
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      ObsoleteSdkInt fires on res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ and advises merging it into
      an unqualified `mipmap-anydpi`, since minSdk 30 already implies v26.

      Do not take that advice: it was tried and it breaks the build. <adaptive-icon>
      is a v26 element, so in an unqualified folder aapt2 does not resolve the
      reference and linking fails with

          AAPT: error: resource mipmap/ic_launcher
          (aka com.iferoporefi.myloyaltycards:mipmap/ic_launcher) not found

      The -v26 qualifier is load-bearing regardless of minSdk.
    -->
    <issue id="ObsoleteSdkInt" severity="ignore">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      DataExtractionRules asks for an `android:fullBackupContent` resource
      alongside `android:dataExtractionRules`, because the latter is ignored
      below Android 12 and minSdk here is 30.

      It is moot for this app: `android:allowBackup="false"` already disables
      backup and restore outright on Android 11, and `fullBackupContent` is only
      consulted when a backup actually runs. Adding the file would be dead config
      that implies backup is enabled when it is not. Android 12+ is covered by
      data_extraction_rules.xml, which excludes root from cloud backup AND from
      device-to-device transfer.
    -->
    <issue id="DataExtractionRules" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      MonochromeLauncherIcon is deliberately NOT suppressed, and it no longer
      fires: Story 21.4 added the <monochrome> layer, so the check is SATISFIED
      rather than silenced. Leaving it live is the point — it is the only thing
      that would notice the layer being dropped again.

      The asset it used to want is generated now, at all four densities, by
      scripts/build-brand-icons.mjs. See README.md § Launcher icon.
    -->
</lint>
